    "title": "How to Watch Oklahoma City Thunder vs. Orlando Magic: NBA Streaming, Tipoff Time, Betting Odds",
    "text": "Shai Gilgeous-Alexander and the Oklahoma City Thunder will hit the road on Tuesday for a matchup against Paolo Banchero and the Orlando Magic.The Thunder come into the game with a 53-15 record, sitting at the top of the Western Conference, most recently defeating Anthony Edwards and the Minnesota Timberwolves 116-103 on Sunday. The Thunder are led by last season's MVP Gilgeous-Alexander, who leads the team with 31.6 points per game and 6.7 assists per game, with All-Star Chet Holmgren leading the team in rebounding at 9.0 per game.AdvertisementThe Magic, on the other hand, go into the matchup with a 38-29 record, good enough for first place in the Southeast Division, and tied with the Miami Heat for the No. 5 seed in the Eastern Conference. Orlando most recently lost to Jalen Johnson and the Atlanta Hawks 124-112 on Monday, snapping the Magic's seven-game winning streak. The Magic are led by Banchero, the former No. 1 overall pick in the 2022 NBA Draft, who leads the team in scoring at 22.2 points per game, with Franz Wagner close behind at 21.3 points per game and Desmond Bane on his trail at 20.6 points per game.Orlando Magic forward Paolo Banchero (5) moves the ball against Los Angeles Lakers guard Luka Doncic Gary A. Vasquez-Imagn Images (Gary A&period; Vasquez-Imagn Images)Thunder vs. Magic Tipoff TimeThunder vs. Magic will tip off on Tuesday at 7:00 p.m. ET. The game will be played at the Kia Center in Orlando, Florida.AdvertisementWhat TV Channel is Thunder vs. Magic on?The matchup between the Thunder vs. Magic will air on FanDuel Sports Network Floridaand FanDuel Sports Network Oklahoma.How to Live Stream Thunder vs. Magic for FreeFans can stream Thunder vs. Magic for free via Fubo when they sign up for a 7-day free trial. The game can also be streamed with an NBA League Pass membership.Thunder vs. Magic Betting OddsSpread: Thunder -9.5 (via ESPN Bet)Over/Under: 222.5Money line: Magic +350, Thunder -455Related: Lakers React to Luka Doncic Announcement on MondayThis story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Mar 17, 2026, where it first appeared in the NBA section. Add Athlon Sports as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
